    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": "The ReProver model uses a <strong>retrieval-augmented tactic generator</strong> to select premises from a large math library. The model takes the current proof state as input and retrieves a ranked list of premises that are likely to be useful for proving the theorem. The retrieved premises are then concatenated with the state and fed into an encoder-decoder Transformer to generate the next tactic.",
